.Dd $Mdocdate: November 5 2026 $
.Dt SIGNET 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm signet
.Nd web authentication system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm help
.Nm
.Cm serve
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Nm
.Cm user-add
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Op Fl hash Ar algorithm
.Op Fl password-stdin
.Ar email
.Op Ar password
.Nm
.Cm user-list
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Nm
.Cm user-approve
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Ar email ...
.Nm
.Cm user-delete
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Fl confirm
.Ar email
.Nm
.Cm webauthn-invite
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Op Fl ttl Ar duration
.Op Fl origin Ar url
.Ar email
.Nm
.Cm user-list-webauthn
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Op Fl email Ar email
.Op Ar email
.Nm
.Cm user-delete-totp
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Op Fl confirm
.Ar email
.Nm
.Cm user-unlock
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Ar email
.Nm
.Cm avatar-remove
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Ar email
.Nm
.Cm user-delete-webauthn
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Fl id Ar credential_id
.Fl confirm
.Nm
.Cm client-add
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Op Fl origins Ar list
.Ar name
.Nm
.Cm client-list
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Nm
.Cm client-revoke
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Ar name
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a web authentication system.
Users sign in with a password, a WebAuthn security key, or a PIN sent by email,
optionally followed by a TOTP code, and receive a signed session cookie.
.Pp
.Nm
reads its configuration from a YAML file
.Po
.Dq config.yaml
by default
.Pc .
See
.Xr signet-config.yaml 5 .
.Pp
.Cm serve
listens for HTTP requests and serves
.Pa /login ,
.Pa /recover ,
.Pa /session
and
.Pa /logout ,
plus the validation API at
.Pa /api/v1/validate .
A successful login is sent to the location given by the
.Va referrer
form field, the
.Cm ?referrer=
query parameter, or the HTTP
.Ev Referer
header, in that order; without any of them it goes to
.Pa / .
Only local paths, URLs on the same host, and URLs on hosts listed in
.Va allowed_redirect_hosts
are accepted.
See
.Xr signet-template 5
for the templates and their variables, and
.Xr signet-api 7
for the HTTP interface.
.Pp
Options must come before positional arguments, and may be written with one
dash or two.
.Pp
.Cm serve
refuses to start until
.Va cookie_secret
is set, and exits non-zero when it cannot start, for example when the listen
address is taken.
Other commands do not need the secret.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options are available for all commands:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl config Ar path
Path to the configuration file.
Default:
.Dq config.yaml .
.El
.Pp
The following options are available for
.Cm user-add :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl hash Ar algorithm
Hash algorithm to use for password hashing.
Must be one of:
.Dq bcrypt ,
.Dq argon2id .
Default:
.Dq argon2id .
.El
.Pp
The following options are available for
.Cm user-delete :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl confirm
Confirm deletion.
Without this flag, the command prints what would be deleted and exits non-zero.
.El
.Pp
The following options are available for
.Cm webauthn-invite :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl ttl Ar duration
How long the link stays valid, for example
.Dq 2h .
Default:
.Dq 24h .
.It Fl origin Ar url
Origin to build the link from.
Default: the first entry of
.Va webauthn_origins .
.El
.Pp
The following options are available for
.Cm user-list-webauthn :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl email Ar email
Email address to list WebAuthn credentials for.
If omitted, the email is taken as the first positional argument.
.El
.Pp
The following options are available for
.Cm user-delete-webauthn :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl id Ar credential_id
The credential ID to delete.
.It Fl confirm
Confirm deletion.
Without this flag, the command prints what would be deleted and exits non-zero.
.El
.Pp
The following options are available for
.Cm client-add :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl origins Ar list
Comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the validation API from
JavaScript.
Only needed when a browser, rather than a server, calls
.Pa /api/v1/validate ;
such calls are answered with CORS headers for the listed origins.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar help
Print a brief usage message and exit.
.It Ar version
Print the version, build time, and git hash, then exit.
.It Ar serve
Start the signet HTTP server.
The server listens on the address configured in
.Xr signet-config.yaml 5
(
.Dq listen ) .
.Pp
The server supports the following signals:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv SIGHUP
Read the configuration file and the templates again, and serve the next
requests by them, without closing the listener
.Po
.Ql rcctl reload signet ,
.Ql systemctl reload signet
.Pc .
A request already being answered finishes as it started.
If the file or a template is wrong, the running configuration stays and the
log says why.
.Va listen ,
.Va protocol ,
.Va socket_mode ,
.Va database_path ,
.Va csv_path
and
.Va log_syslog
take effect only at a restart; a reload keeps them and logs which changed.
Rate-limit counts kept in memory start over; the account lockout, sessions and
everything else in the database stay.
.It Dv SIGTERM , Dv SIGINT
Graceful shutdown.
.El
.It Ar user-add Ar email Op Ar password
Add a new user to the CSV user store.
If
.Ar password
is not provided, the account has no password and cannot use password sign-in;
it can sign in with an emailed PIN or with a key enrolled through
.Cm webauthn-invite ,
and it can set a password through password recovery.
A password given as an argument can be seen by
.Xr ps 1
and is kept in shell history, so
.Cm user-add
warns when it is given that way.
.Fl password-stdin
reads it from the first line of standard input instead; only the line ending is
removed, an empty line is an error, and giving an argument as well is an error.
.Pp
The user is created with the
.Dq approved
flag.
.Ar email
must be one plain
.Li local@domain ,
not a list, a name or a quoted local part.
Addresses match without regard to case, so an address that differs from an
existing account only in case is refused.
The commands that take an
.Ar email
find the account the same way.
.It Ar user-list
List all users in the CSV store.
.It Ar user-approve Ar email ...
Add the
.Dq approved
flag.
While
.Va self_registration_approval
is
.Dq required ,
an account with
.Dq self_registered
and without
.Dq approved
cannot sign in by any method.
Accounts created by
.Cm user-add
by older versions carry
.Dq self_registered
and need this command once.
.It Ar user-delete Ar email
Delete an account, its sessions, its WebAuthn credentials and TOTP keys, its
picture, any invite and any recovery link.
Requires
.Fl confirm .
Removing a row from the CSV file by hand, or setting the
.Dq locked
flag, stops new logins but leaves existing sessions valid until they expire.
.It Ar webauthn-invite Ar email
Print a one-time link that enrolls a security key on the account without
signing in, for accounts with no other way to sign in.
The account must already exist.
A new invite replaces any earlier one for that address.
It refuses when the configuration has WebAuthn off.
The token is in the URL fragment, so it does not reach web-server logs;
send the link over a channel you trust, since anyone holding it can add a key.
.It Ar user-list-webauthn Op Ar email
List WebAuthn credentials for a user, with each one's attestation format and
whether it may be backed up, as a synced passkey may.
If
.Ar email
is not provided as an argument, use
.Fl email .
.It Ar user-delete-totp Ar email
Remove every TOTP key and recovery code of an account, for someone who has lost
their authenticator and their recovery codes.
Signing in then asks for no code until a new key is added.
Requires
.Fl confirm .
.It Ar user-unlock Ar email
Clear the account's count of failed sign-ins, ending a lock by
.Va account_lockout_threshold
.Pq see Xr signet-config.yaml 5 .
A finished sign-in, by any method, or a password recovery clears it as well.
.It Ar avatar-remove Ar email
Remove the account's picture, which then stops being served.
The account can set a new one, if
.Va avatars
is enabled.
.It Ar user-delete-webauthn
Delete a WebAuthn credential and end every session of its account, however each
one signed in, so that whoever used the key does not stay signed in.
Requires
.Fl id
and
.Fl confirm .
.It Ar client-add Ar name
Register an application allowed to call
.Pa /api/v1/validate ,
and print its API key.
The key is shown once; only its hash is stored.
.It Ar client-list
List registered applications, their allowed origins and creation time.
.It Ar client-revoke Ar name
Delete a registered application.
Its API key stops working immediately.
.El
.Sh FILES
Without
.Fl config ,
commands read
.Pa /etc/signet/config.yaml
when signet comes from the
.Ox
or Debian package, or the Docker image,
.Pa /usr/local/etc/signet/config.yaml
from the
.Fx
package, and
.Pa config.yaml
in the current directory when it is built from source.
The file holds
.Va cookie_secret ,
so keep it unreadable by other users.
.Cm serve
logs a warning when this file, the CSV file or the database is world-readable.
.Pp
The data directory is
.Pa /var/www/signet
on
.Ox
and
.Pa /var/lib/signet
on Debian and Linux, and
.Pa /var/db/signet
on
.Fx .
The Debian package keeps the working copies of the web files in
.Pa /etc/signet/templates
and
.Pa /etc/signet/static ,
and the shipped ones in
.Pa /usr/share/signet/web ;
the
.Fx
package in
.Pa /usr/local/etc/signet
and
.Pa /usr/local/share/signet/web .
.Pp
Example configurations ship under
.Pa /usr/local/share/examples/signet
on
.Ox
(and
.Pa /usr/share/doc/signet/examples
on Linux): a sample
.Pa config.yaml ,
the web templates and static files, example claims hooks in
.Pa hooks/ ,
and web-server sample configs in
.Pa web-servers/
for Caddy, nginx, and
.Ox
.Xr httpd 8 .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Add a new user with a password, kept out of the process list and shell
history:
.Pp
.Dl signet user-add -password-stdin alice@example.com < password-file
.Pp
Start the server:
.Pp
.Dl signet serve
.Pp
List all users:
.Pp
.Dl signet user-list
.Pp
Start the server with a custom config:
.Pp
.Dl signet serve -config /etc/signet/config.yaml
.Pp
Approve a self-registered account:
.Pp
.Dl signet user-approve alice@example.com
.Pp
Delete an account with its sessions and security keys:
.Pp
.Dl signet user-delete -confirm alice@example.com
.Pp
Print a one-time link, valid for two hours, to enroll a security key:
.Pp
.Dl signet webauthn-invite -ttl 2h alice@example.com
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr signet-config.yaml 5 ,
.Xr signet-hooks 5 ,
.Xr signet-template 5 ,
.Xr signet-api 7
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was first released in 2026.
.Sh CAVEATS
Removing an account from the CSV file by hand, or setting its
.Dq locked
flag, stops new logins but leaves existing sessions valid until they expire.
Use
.Cm user-delete
to end them.
